      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The sudden onset of the sensation can be attributed to the rapid release and concentration of syn-propanethial-S-oxide gas in the air, which then comes into contact with the moisture on the surface of the eyes. This interaction causes the gas to diffuse through the tear film and bind to the olfactory receptors in the cornea and conjunctiva, sending a strong signal to the nervous system that is perceived as a sharp, pungent sting. The syn-propanethial-S-oxide gas is more soluble in water when it's in the vapor state, allowing it to penetrate the tear film quickly and effectively, contributing to the sudden and intense feeling of irritation.",
